<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tt xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xml:lang="en">
  <body>
    <div>
      <p begin="00:00:00.690" end="00:00:05.690">Who hasn't recorded a script at some point in their life?</p>
      <p begin="00:00:05.690" end="00:00:10.690">That is why we have created Table Read Tools,</p>
      <p begin="00:00:10.690" end="00:00:15.690">a new way of looking at your scripts.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:15.690" end="00:00:23.530">First of all, we assign an image to each character.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:34.290" end="00:00:37.290">Then you arrange them by importance.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:41.190" end="00:00:42.190">That's good.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:43.290" end="00:00:46.290">Then we go to locations</p>
      <p begin="00:00:46.690" end="00:00:48.690">and add the locations.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:53.290" end="00:00:55.290">Here is one.</p>
      <p begin="00:00:56.390" end="00:00:57.850">And the next one.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:02.960" end="00:01:07.960">And once you have everything ready, we move to the conversation module.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:08.960" end="00:01:13.960">From now on, you can see your scripts as if they were a chat conversation.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:15.960" end="00:01:21.960">It shows you the character who is speaking and the script time elapsed.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:22.960" end="00:01:25.960">Or you can view it as a script reading.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:26.960" end="00:01:30.800">You see the space where the scene takes place and then</p>
      <p begin="00:01:31.800" end="00:01:35.800">Let the magic happen by itself.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:35.800" end="00:01:40.800">The dialogues automatically move from one character to another</p>
      <p begin="00:01:40.800" end="00:01:46.800">with an approximate calculation of the time needed for someone to read them.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:46.800" end="00:01:54.800">You can run it automatically or move forward manually.</p>
      <p begin="00:01:59.280" end="00:02:10.000">You can export the photographs to apply them to other projects if you have the same actors</p>
      <p begin="00:02:10.000" end="00:02:15.120">And that's it, a new way of looking at your scripts.</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</tt>
